{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/95608-ghost-fighting-and-other-advice","id":95608,"title":"Ghost fighting and other advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-21T07:30:36-07:00","id":95608,"title":"Ghost fighting and other advice","content":"I am currently creating a one-shot game for Geist based on the events in Russia and Ukraine. I am still new to creating these adventures so I would like some help creating it. The event I will be running it at takes place in Raleigh NC so if you are attending events there and are interested stop reading now to avoid spoilers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The main advice I need is on ghost battles, how do they work? I can't seem to find anything in the corebook but I may just be overlooking it. I also need advice on enemies. I plan to make pre-gens with 70 exp points so how can I make enemies that are tough but won't cause my players to die? Dieing like swooping is bad. (Cookie to whoever gets the reference) <br /> <br /> I will also attach my current outline so you can see how the game starts and offer advice.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> OUTLINE:<br /> <br /> ACT I<br /> The group awakens in the ruins of a plane it is very cold and snow is falling all around them. They all have a vivid vision of the person who died in their place a wits + politics roll will reveal that their replacements died at the hands of a Russian soldier. <br /> If the group decides to search the plane\u2019s ruins they will have to make a wits + investigation roll to look for information and wits + survival to look for supplies.<br /> <br /> <b>Information</b>:<br /> 1 success, they find several bodies with Latvian passports revealing that they likely crashed in Latvia.<br /> 2 successes they find a newspaper article on tensions between Latvia and Rusia over dig rights at a recently found ruin.<br /> 3+ successes they find all of the above plus an iphone turned to an internet page announcing an all-out invasion of Latvia by Russian troops.<br /> Exceptional success: they find a dying pilot who tells them the plane was shot down by a missile.<br /> <b>Survival </b><br /> <br /> 1 success: they find a large blanket that can be used to keep warm while resting<br /> <br /> 2 successes: they find a large map including their flight path so they can approximate their location<br /> 3+ all of the above plus a gps system that gives them their exact location<br /> Exceptional success: they find a survival kit including a flare gun, a .22 rifle and large survival knife.<br /> They can try as long as they want to make these checks but must deal with exposure checks every 2 turns and after 5 turns soldiers will set upon them.<br /> <b>Soldier encounter:</b><br /> A wits + politics (1 success) roll will let them realize that the soilders are not Russian but are actually some type of Latvian militia. An exceptional success will reveal that they are a pro-democracy miltia and woul be very friendly toward Americans.<br /> <br /> Wits + empathy (2 successes) can tell that they are there to investigate the crash and aren\u2019t hostile\u2026 yet. An exceptional success will reveal that they will help if asked to.<br /> Wits + investigation (3 successes) will reveal that none of them have the required equipment to shoot down a plane. An exceptional success will reveal that they are not well trained with weapons either.<br /> If one of the two pregens with Russian language is used they will be able to talk with them, otherwise it will take3 successes on a wits + socialize check to communicate to them.<br /> Even if they fail their communication check they will receive an option to follow the militia they must either follow or fight them.<br /> Fight: two of the three soldiers carries an AK-47, one a shotgun if the party wins they must navigate the rest of the way through the forest to a town.<br /> <b>The Town</b><br /> The group finds its way to a small town or is lead there by the militia. A graveyard is prominent in the town and several tombstones are marked. A wits + occult roll will let them read it on the fly or intelligence + occult if they go up and look closely. The markings warn that sin eaters in the area are being hunted. If asked a local will tell them the marking went up soon after the coup that deposed Putin. The group can attempt to leave a message on the tomstones with an Int + occult roll.<br /> <br /> By now it is late at night and they need to find a place to sleep, unfortuently there is no place so they will have to sleep in a drainage pipe for the night and make resolve + stamina checks to avoid 2 points of bashing damage and -1 penalties to all rolls. If they succeded in the roll to leave a twilight network message they will not have to stay there long enough to gain the penalties.<br /> While sleeping they are roused by the sound of someone approaching. The man who approaches is a Sin Eater as is obvious by his frog like Geist. <br /> <br /> (there was a coup and Putin has been replaced by a General who is being advised and ultimately controlled by a vengeful ghost perhaps Rasputin the general is killing off sin eaters<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}